          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ExoticBoundary7Spheres With exotic boundary 7-spheres
          %p
            Consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4
            denote the 4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
            regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            is an 8-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} manifold with boundary
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of maps
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_{(m,n)}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  S^3
                  \\longrightarrow
                  SO(4)
          %p
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equator"} equator
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%284%29"} SO(4)
            %a{:href => "SO4#TheExceptionalIso"} this Prop.
            such maps are classified by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m,n) \in \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            If here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo ±
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m+n = \pm 1
            then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-manifold"} 8-manifold
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalent"} homotopy equivalent
            to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
          %p
            Assuming this 8-manifold is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+genus"} signature
            formula
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SignatureFormula"} (1)
            yields the relation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 7
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi m
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 45
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p_2[X]
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{7}
                  \\big(
                  4(2m -1)^2 + 45
                  \\big)
          %p
            Here the left hand side must be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m,n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
            to the standard smooth 7-sphere – it is instead an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+7-sphere"} exotic 7-sphere
          %p
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JoachimWraith"} Joachim-Wraith, p. 2-3
          %p
            From the point of view of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+8-manifolds"} M-theory on 8-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/8-manifolds"} 8-manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with (exotic)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+limits"} near horizon limits
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2+brane"} M2 brane
            spacetimes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1} \times X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            themselves would be sitting at the center of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-spheres"} 7-spheres
            (if that were included in the spacetime, see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MorrisonPlesser99"}> Morrison-Plesser 99, section 3.2
